  "Question": "Find the number of two-digit positive integers whose digits total \\(7.\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\)",
    "B": "\\(7\\)",
    "C": "\\(8\\)",
    "D": "\\(9\\)",
    "E": "\\(10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "A two-digit number has a tens digit of at least \\(1\\). Because the digits total \\(7\\) and the ones digit cannot be negative, the tens digit can only be \\(1,2,3,4,5,6,\\) or \\(7\\).\n\nFor each tens digit, subtract it from \\(7\\) to get the only possible ones digit. This gives\n\\[\n16,\\ 25,\\ 34,\\ 43,\\ 52,\\ 61,\\ 70.\n\\]\nEvery possible tens digit has been included, and different tens digits give different numbers. Thus the list counts every valid number exactly once. There are \\(7\\) integers, choice B.",
